OL,3,GNEWSAVolunteers aim to sew town's
OL,4,A1,200-year history
OL,5,
OL,6,FVolunteers are working on an
OL,7,Fembroidered timeline to record a town's
OL,8,F1,200-year history.
OL,10,FThe Friends of St Cuthbert's Church,
OL,11,FBillingham, commissioned six panels
OL,12,Fdepicting the "tiny little church on
OL,13,Fthe hill" in the 9th century, through
OL,14,Fto the town's industrialisation and the
OL,15,Finflux of people coming to work in
OL,16,Fshipbuilding and chemicals.
OL,18,FVolunteer Jackie Ward said the story
OL,19,Fremained relevant because "without the
OL,20,Feconomic migrants, the town really
OL,21,Fwouldn't have become what it is now".
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
